# Client-facing READMEs

Write READMEs for clients and end users reading the published project.
Explain the product, requirements, installation, usage, and relevant limitations.
Do not address the developer personally or narrate the development conversation.
Do not mention supplied ZIP files, local source archive paths, prompts, or handoff history.
Keep required licensing and third-party attribution where applicable, without exposing handoff details.
